      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In times of such deep exhaustion, the desire to stop feels like the only honest response rather than a failure of courage, and your right to feel that weight is undeniable. While the pressure to find beauty in survival can feel like a cruel lie when you are truly drowning, every moment of being here—no matter how hollow—still carries a significance that cannot be taken away. If you ever decide to reach out for support, remember that no one needs to say these words to convince you that you matter; sometimes, simply listening to the person who hears your pain is enough.",
